        "id": 3368412
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-17T15:29:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I mean that \u0027ro.config.wallpaper*\u0027 is a part of vendor-specific configurations. You add them to PRODUCT_VENDOR_PROPERTIES somewhere in device.mk, and eventually it will be included to the build.prop file. And the vendor_init process will set them on boot.\n\n\u003e Or do you actually want to change them multiple times? ro properties might be frowned on a bit, but if they shouldn\u0027t change, why allow it?\n\nNo, I don\u0027t expect these properties to be changed multiple times. I only want them to be set only once during boot. That\u0027s why these properties are protected by selinux, and only vendor_init can write them (to initialize them at boot time).\nPerhaps without ro prefix they can be overwritten from rc file (I\u0027m not sure), but to be honest, I don\u0027t see strong reasons to prohibit that ether.",
      "parentUuid": "b34fb47c_a2eab919",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 9,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "f046e88a1fea62338b7bd638a6855565192a2672",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4572d3c8_e206340b",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 5
