    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "86df6b1f_7c1fce92",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 11,
      "author": {
        "id": 3368412
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-09-17T15:29:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e It sounds like it might not be possible\n\nIf I\u0027m wrong and the old properties are not broken in the current codebase, it would be even better. It would mean that this patch is simply modernizing the code a little.\n\n\n\u003e there is a backwards compatibility concern here\n\nAs far as I understand, not really.\nBecause the sepolicy for the \u0027ro.config.wallpaper*\u0027 properties has been broken since approximately AOSP 12, we have only three types of vendors:\n 1. vendor who use AOSP 11 or earlier\n 2. vendor who define their own vendor-specific selinux rules for \u0027ro.config.wallpaper\u0027 to make it work\n 3. vendor who don\u0027t use \u0027ro.config.wallpaper\u0027 at all\n\nThe only compatibility problem I see may be in the first situation, if someone decides to upgrade firmware for some device from AOSP11 to AOSP15+. But in this case, it looks like it will not be a problem for vendors to start using new property names.\n\n\n\u003e the properties are removed\n\nThe old properties are still used as \u0027legacy_prop_name\u0027 (as a fallback).",
      "parentUuid": "4572d3c8_e206340b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 11,
        "endChar": 48
      },
      "revId": "f046e88a1fea62338b7bd638a6855565192a2672",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
